3DSMax have the notion of "Layers" to organize nodes by group (not in a hierarchical way), and Blender have the same principle named "Collections".

I need to generate FBX files with nodes associated to layers. It's pretty straightforward in FBX side (extracts are from `test/models/FBX/box_orphant_embedded_texture.fbx`):
* Declare a new object type in the header:
```
	ObjectType: "CollectionExclusive" {
		Count: 1
		PropertyTemplate: "FbxDisplayLayer" {
			Properties70:  {
				P: "Color", "ColorRGB", "Color", "",0.8,0.8,0.8
				P: "Show", "bool", "", "",1
				P: "Freeze", "bool", "", "",0
				P: "LODBox", "bool", "", "",0
			}
		}
	}
```
* Add a "CollectionExclusive / DisplayLayer" object per layer
```
	CollectionExclusive: 2959111896352, "DisplayLayer::Box", "DisplayLayer" {
		Properties70:  {
			P: "Color", "ColorRGB", "Color", "",0.607999980449677,0,0.157000005245209
		}
	}
```
* Associate nodes to layers, and link sub-layers togethers:
```
	;Model::Box, DisplayLayer::Box
	C: "OO",2957618625584,2959111896352
```

So, pretty easy, neah? The problem I have is how to handle this additional information on Assimp side. I see two solutions:
* The simpler/faster is to add a custom metadata to aiNode (need a common metadata id for this?)
* Add a `aiLayer` object to API, and add a `aiLayer* rootLayer` object to `aiScene`, it's a lot more work and a potential API break :/

As you see, neither of the 2 proposal are perfect, what do you think?

**Describe the bug**
glTF2 Asset::FindUniqueID() is ridiculously slow.
Export takes a whole minute instead of a fraction of a second.

**To Reproduce**
Export a model with e.g. a significant large number of meshes.

**Expected behavior**
Asset::FindUniqueID() should complete in O(log(n)) time.

This loop (https://github.com/assimp/assimp/blob/master/code/AssetLib/glTF2/glTF2Asset.inl#L1726):
```c++
    int offset = ai_snprintf(buffer.data(), buffer.size(), "%s_", id.c_str());
    for (int i = 0; it != mUsedIds.end(); ++i) {
        ai_snprintf(buffer.data() + offset, buffer.size() - offset, "%d", i);
        id = buffer.data();
        it = mUsedIds.find(id);
    }
```

loops through every single entry in the map of ids, every single time an id is added, and do a lookup as well on each and every single entry. This is a huge problem.

All that is needed as a fix is something as simple as:

```c++
    int offset = ai_snprintf(buffer.data(), buffer.size(), "%s_%d", id.c_str(), lastId++);
    id = buffer.data();

    /* This is ridiculously slow and overkill...
    for (int i = 0; it != mUsedIds.end(); ++i) {
        ai_snprintf(buffer.data() + offset, buffer.size() - offset, "%d", i);
        id = buffer.data();
        it = mUsedIds.find(id);
    }*/
```
with `int lastId;` added as a member of `class Asset`.

Also the `__GNUC___` check had an extra underscore afterwards, is that intended?

https://github.com/assimp/assimp/blob/master/code/AssetLib/glTF2/glTF2Asset.h#L88

AFAIK the proper preprocessor definition is with only two underscores:
```
#if _MSC_VER > 1500 || defined(__GNUC__)
#       define ASSIMP_GLTF_USE_UNORDERED_MULTIMAP
```

